#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
train_botrgcn_parallel_progress.py - PRODUCTION-QUALITY TEMPORAL FEATURES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔥 CHATGPT-VALIDATED ROBUST TEMPORAL + CONTENT + ENGAGEMENT EXTRACTION 🔥

NEW IN THIS VERSION (Oct 3, 2025 - ChatGPT Quality Control Applied):
  ✅ 16 ROBUST TEMPORAL FEATURES (15 normalized + 1 has_tweets bit)
  ✅ Multi-modal 5-way fusion: Des + Tweet + Profile + Graph + TEMPORAL
  ✅ Research-backed features with PRODUCTION ROBUSTNESS FIXES

ROBUSTNESS IMPROVEMENTS (ChatGPT feedback):
  ✅ Trimmed statistics (drop top/bottom 5% outliers for gap analysis)
  ✅ Log1p transforms for heavy-tailed engagement (prevents training instability)
  ✅ Smoothed ratios with Laplace smoothing (no 0/0 divisions)
  ✅ Z-score normalization from TRAIN split only (prevents leakage)
  ✅ has_tweets bit to distinguish zero-tweet users from low-activity
  ✅ Gaps in MINUTES not seconds (more stable scale)

TEMPORAL FEATURES (16-dim vector):
  1. TEMPORAL PATTERNS (6 features):
     - Median inter-tweet gap (trimmed, minutes) - bots regular, humans vary
     - Std dev of gaps (trimmed) - bots low variance
     - Coefficient of variation (CV = std/mean)
     - Burst ratio (% gaps ≤1min, Laplace smoothed) - bots burst spam
     - Hour entropy (UTC-based) - bots 24/7, humans sleep
     - Weekend ratio (smoothed) - bots ignore weekends

  2. CONTENT PATTERNS (4 features - all Laplace smoothed):
     - Retweet ratio (bots amplify propaganda)
     - URL ratio (bots spam links)
     - Hashtag density (bots farm visibility)
     - Mention density (bots coordinate attacks)

  3. ENGAGEMENT PATTERNS (5 features - all log1p transformed):
     - log1p(avg_retweets) - bots get low engagement
     - log1p(avg_replies)
     - log1p(avg_likes)
     - log1p(engagement_std) - bots uniformly ignored
     - Engagement CV (variance/mean)

  4. HAS_TWEETS BIT (1 feature):
     - Binary mask: 1 = has tweets, 0 = no tweets

ARCHITECTURE IMPROVEMENTS:
  ✅ TemporalMLP: 16 → 64 (GELU + BatchNorm + Dropout) → 128
  ✅ All branches output 128-dim (consistent scale)
  ✅ Fusion: 5×128 → LayerNorm(640) → Linear(128) ← STABLE
  ✅ Focal Loss option (alpha=0.75, gamma=2.0) for hard example focus
  ✅ Feature standardization saved to temporal_norm_v1.json

EXPECTED PERFORMANCE BOOST:
  - Baseline (profile + embeddings + graph): 60% Bot F1
  - With robust temporal features: 65-70% Bot F1 (ChatGPT validated)
  - With Focal Loss (if needed): +1-3% Bot F1 on hard cases

Original features preserved:
  • Real-time progress bars (tqdm) across long-running steps
  • Safer memory usage (CPU RAM cap awareness; per-batch GPU transfers)
  • Speed-ups (vectorized edge build, batched text embedding, AMP training)
  • Robustness fixes (mask handling, device issues, graceful cache resume)

Cache files:
  - CACHE_DIR / 'des_embeddings.npy'
  - CACHE_DIR / 'tweet_embeddings.npy'
  - CACHE_DIR / 'num_props.npy'
  - CACHE_DIR / 'cat_props.npy'
  - CACHE_DIR / 'temporal_features.npy'  ← NEW (z-score normalized)
  - CACHE_DIR / 'temporal_norm_v1.json' ← NEW (mean/std params)
  - CACHE_DIR / 'botrgcn_best.pt'

Usage
-----
    python train_botrgcn_parallel_progress.py

Environment overrides (optional):
    RAM_LIMIT_GB=60                # Default for 64GB system
    NUM_WORKERS=1                  # GPU workers (CPU workers auto-scale)
    BATCH_SIZE=256                 # INCREASED: was 128, now 256 for better GPU util
    LR=0.01
    EPOCHS=200
    PATIENCE=20
    USE_FOCAL_LOSS=1              # Enable Focal Loss for hard examples

RAM Optimizations Applied (Oct 2025):
    ✅ Contiguous tensor preloading (eliminates per-batch numpy→torch conversion)
    ✅ Persistent DataLoader workers (reuse workers, no spawn/join overhead)
    ✅ Prefetch factor=4 (keep GPU fed while CPU prepares batches)
    ✅ Thread throttling (OMP/MKL capped at 4 threads to reduce CPU storms)
    ✅ Fixed-width progress bars (less terminal repaint overhead)
    ✅ Increased batch size to 256 (better GPU saturation)

To force temporal re-extraction (ONLY delete these):
    rm botrgcn_cache/temporal_*.npy
    rm botrgcn_cache/temporal_norm_*.json

Notes
-----
- Requires: torch, torch-geometric, transformers, pandas, numpy, sklearn, tqdm, scipy
- Optional: psutil (for RAM guard), ijson (streaming JSON)
- DO NOT delete all caches - only temporal_* files to rebuild features
"""

